<Brushes>

  <!-- Difficulty screen dropdown reskin, THIRD approach (2026-09-30) - the first two both overrode NATIVE
       brush names (SPOptions.Dropdown.*/Standard.DropdownItem), which turned out to be globally shared: the
       main menu's own unrelated Options screen uses the same native widget/brush names, so that override broke
       options there too (user: "I now dont see some options anymore in the my options from the main menu") and
       had to be fully reverted. This time: TAOMDropdown.xml (Prefabs folder) is a full PRIVATE COPY of the
       native Standard.DropdownWithHorizontalControl.xml, referenced only from TAOMOptionsStage.xml, whose
       internal brush references are all renamed to this "TAOM.Dropdown.*" prefix below - names nothing else in
       the game could ever resolve to, so this can't leak anywhere else again. Same visual design as the
       earlier (confirmed-working) attempt: fs_dropdown_box_9 (own asset, gold border) for the box/extension,
       FS_Garamond for the value/item text (distinct from the CC.SecTitle header label above it), AI-generated
       gold arrow glyphs (ImagineArt) for the prev/next buttons, and a gold hover wash for list items. Arrow
       sprites re-cropped 2026-09-30 (user: "the arrows seem sort of silly") - the button they fill is a fixed
       60x70 box, and the first crop's own aspect didn't match that, so the brush's fill-the-widget stretch
       squished a clean chevron into a diamond-ish blob; re-cropped onto a canvas matching that exact 60:70
       ratio (content itself keeps ITS OWN proportions, just padded within the matching canvas) so no more
       stretch-distortion. Plain sprites now (no .nine) - nine-slicing them earlier was only ever a hypothesis
       test for a bug that turned out to be the cross-screen brush collision, not something these actually
       need. -->
  <!-- FIX (2026-10-01, user real-screenshot report: the box showed a light woven/cross-hatch texture instead
       of a clean dark fill, even after a full restart confirmed the brush itself was resolving). fs_dropdown_box_9
       was a genuine PNG stretched via 9-slice across a much wider box than it was drawn for - swapped to
       BlankWhiteSquare_9 (a flat, dither-free native sprite already proven artifact-free at any stretch width,
       same one used for the checkbox/Narrative option rows/Banner Editor slider) with an explicit dark Color
       tint standing in for the old baked-in dark PNG color. Same Style/ColorFactor feedback kept unchanged. -->
  <!-- FIX (2026-10-03, Custom Battle report: these 4 brushes rendered as a plain unstyled grey/white box in
       TAOM_CustomBattle, while this exact TAOMDropdown.xml prefab is confirmed working on the Options/
       Difficulty screen in TAOM_FactionUI, and brand-new brushes using a simpler always-visible-layer pattern
       (TAOM.CB.Slider.Fill etc.) rendered correctly in the SAME Custom Battle screen. The one structural
       difference: these 4 used an "IsHidden=true on the base layer, each Style reveals it" indirection
       (copied from native CustomBattle.Slider.* brushes) that every other working brush in this project does
       NOT use. Simplified to the same plain "layer always visible, Style only adjusts ColorFactor/AlphaFactor"
       technique as everything else - removes the one real structural outlier rather than guessing further. -->
  <!-- FIX round 2 (2026-10-03): still showed a missing-texture checkerboard in Custom Battle after dropping
       IsHidden. The one remaining difference from the proven-working TAOM.CB.Slider.* brushes: these had
       ExtendTop/Bottom/Left/Right="10" nine-slice attributes stacked on top of the "_9" sprite variant - the
       slider brushes use a plain stretch with no Extend at all. BlankWhiteSquare_9 is a flat solid-color
       swatch, so nine-slicing adds no visual value anyway (no border art to preserve) - dropped entirely,
       converging on the exact same plain-stretch technique already confirmed rendering correctly. -->
  <!-- FIX (2026-10-03, user real screenshot: "the background of those selectors should be transparent so you
       can see the stone texture behind it") - this is the CLOSED dropdown box specifically (a different brush
       from TAOM.Dropdown.Item.Text/TAOM.DropdownItem, which only affect the OPEN list after clicking - that's
       why the earlier Narrative-style fix didn't show up here). Was fully opaque (no AlphaFactor at all, same
       as a solid black box). Added AlphaFactor so the panel's own cc_panel_bg stone texture shows through,
       matching the frameless language used elsewhere in this project, while staying dark enough for the gold
       text to stay readable. -->
  <Brush Name="TAOM.Dropdown.Center">
    <Layers>
      <BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="BlankWhiteSquare_9" Color="#14120DFF" />
    </Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="0.85" AlphaFactor="0.45" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="0.7" AlphaFactor="0.6" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="1.3" AlphaFactor="0.6" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="0.6" AlphaFactor="0.4" /></Style>
    </Styles>
    <SoundProperties>
      <EventSounds>
        <EventSound EventName="Click" Audio="dropdown" />
      </EventSounds>
    </SoundProperties>
  </Brush>
  <!-- Same transparency fix as TAOM.Dropdown.Center above, kept a bit more opaque (0.75 vs 0.45) since this
       is the OPEN list background - several stacked lines of text need more contrast than a single closed-box
       line does. -->
  <Brush Name="TAOM.Dropdown.Extension">
    <Layers>
      <BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="BlankWhiteSquare_9" Color="#14120DFF" />
    </Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="0.95" AlphaFactor="0.75" /></Style>
    </Styles>
  </Brush>
  <Brush Name="TAOM.Dropdown.Left.Button">
    <Layers>
      <BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="fs_dropdown_arrow_left" />
    </Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.85" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="0.8" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="1.2" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.4" /></Style>
    </Styles>
    <SoundProperties>
      <EventSounds>
        <EventSound EventName="Click" Audio="dropdown" />
      </EventSounds>
    </SoundProperties>
  </Brush>
  <Brush Name="TAOM.Dropdown.Right.Button">
    <Layers>
      <BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="fs_dropdown_arrow_right" />
    </Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.85" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="0.8" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="1.2" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.4" /></Style>
    </Styles>
    <SoundProperties>
      <EventSounds>
        <EventSound EventName="Click" Audio="dropdown" />
      </EventSounds>
    </SoundProperties>
  </Brush>
  <Brush Name="TAOM.Dropdown.Center.Text" Font="FS_Garamond" FontSize="16" TextVerticalAlignment="Center">
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default" FontColor="#F2E2B0FF" TextGlowColor="#000000A0" TextGlowRadius="0.1" TextBlur="0.05" />
      <Style Name="Disabled" FontColor="#F2E2B080" TextGlowColor="#00000000" />
    </Styles>
  </Brush>
  <!-- Dropdown list items restyled to match Narrative Stage's own option-row language (2026-10-03, user
       request) - see TAOMDropdown.xml's own comment on its item template for the full story. Color values
       copied exactly from CC.NarrativeOption/CC.NarrativeOptionAccent, not just "similar" ones, so the two
       screens' selectors genuinely read as the same design language. -->
  <Brush Name="TAOM.Dropdown.Item.Text" Font="FS_Garamond" FontSize="16" TextHorizontalAlignment="Left">
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default" FontColor="#8F8670FF" TextGlowColor="#000000B0" TextGlowRadius="0.1" TextBlur="0.05" />
      <Style Name="Hovered" FontColor="#EFE7D2FF" TextGlowColor="#000000B0" TextGlowRadius="0.1" TextBlur="0.05" />
      <Style Name="Selected" FontColor="#F6E7B4FF" TextGlowColor="#000000C0" TextGlowRadius="0.15" TextBlur="0.05" />
      <Style Name="Disabled" FontColor="#8F867080" TextGlowColor="#00000000" />
    </Styles>
  </Brush>
  <Brush Name="TAOM.DropdownItem">
    <Layers><BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="BlankWhiteSquare_9" Color="#F6E7B4FF" /></Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.3" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.6" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Selected"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0" /></Style>
    </Styles>
  </Brush>
  <!-- FIX (2026-10-01, user real-screenshot report: "Enable Birth and Aging" checkbox rendered as a plain
       unstyled white square even after a full restart). Root cause found by diffing against
       Native\GUI\Prefabs\CharCreation\CharacterCreationOptionsStage.xml: the native checkbox's outer
       ButtonWidget ALWAYS carries a Brush (SPOptions.Checkbox.Empty.Button); our reskin's version
       (TAOMOptionsStage.xml) dropped Brush= entirely, relying only on loose hand-built child widgets for the
       visual, on the assumption a ButtonWidget with no Brush just renders nothing of its own. It doesn't - with
       no Brush at all it appears to fall back to some native default placeholder (a plain white square) drawn
       over/instead of the children. This brush is a permanently-invisible placeholder (every style keeps
       AlphaFactor 0) so the ButtonWidget has "a Brush" to satisfy whatever internal check wants one, while every
       real visual (dark fill, gold border bars, gold toggle square) stays exactly as already built, unchanged,
       via the loose children. -->
  <Brush Name="TAOM.Checkbox.Empty">
    <Layers><BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="BlankWhiteSquare_9" AlphaFactor="0" /></Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0" /></Style>
    </Styles>
  </Brush>
  <!-- Character creation skin (face generator and later stages). Gold #C9AB69/#D6BA75, cream #EFE7D2, near black panels. Fonts: this module's FS_* fonts. -->

  <Brush Name="CC.Title" Font="FS_CinzelWide" FontSize="26" TextHorizontalAlignment="Center" TextVerticalAlignment="Center">
    <Styles><Style Name="Default" FontColor="#EFE7D2FF" TextGlowColor="#000000B0" TextGlowRadius="0.15" TextBlur="0.1" /></Styles>
  </Brush>

  <Brush Name="CC.Label" Font="FS_CinzelWide" FontSize="17" TextHorizontalAlignment="Center" TextVerticalAlignment="Center">
    <Styles><Style Name="Default" FontColor="#D9CBA0FF" TextGlowColor="#000000B0" TextGlowRadius="0.15" TextBlur="0.1" /></Styles>
  </Brush>

  <Brush Name="CC.Value" Font="FS_CinzelWide" FontSize="20" TextHorizontalAlignment="Center" TextVerticalAlignment="Center">
    <Styles><Style Name="Default" FontColor="#EFE7D2FF" TextGlowColor="#000000A0" TextGlowRadius="0.1" TextBlur="0.05" /></Styles>
  </Brush>

  <Brush Name="CC.KeyText" Font="FS_Garamond" FontSize="20" TextHorizontalAlignment="Left" TextVerticalAlignment="Center">
    <Styles><Style Name="Default" FontColor="#E9E1CCFF" /></Styles>
  </Brush>

  <!-- Sized/muted down 2026-09-26 (user request: "more subtle, so it looks more elegant, bit smaller") - was
       22pt at near-white E6DDC2 with a strong glow, reading more like a loading-screen tip than a quiet
       decorative accent. FontSize 22->16, color dimmed and given a lower alpha (CC instead of FF) rather than
       just a darker opaque color, glow softened to match (radius/alpha both reduced) so it recedes into the
       scene instead of competing with the actual UI content. -->
  <Brush Name="CC.Quote" Font="FS_CinzelWide" FontSize="16" TextHorizontalAlignment="Left" TextVerticalAlignment="Top">
    <Styles><Style Name="Default" FontColor="#D9CFAECC" TextGlowColor="#00000090" TextGlowRadius="0.12" TextBlur="0.12" /></Styles>
  </Brush>

  <Brush Name="CC.QuoteSub" Font="FS_Garamond" FontSize="13" TextHorizontalAlignment="Left" TextVerticalAlignment="Top">
    <Styles><Style Name="Default" FontColor="#9C9478AA" TextGlowColor="#00000090" TextGlowRadius="0.12" TextBlur="0.12" /></Styles>
  </Brush>

  <!-- top ribbon text tabs (2026-09-23 redesign, replaces the CC.Tab.* icon-medallion brushes below - those are
       kept, unused, in case any future round wants icons back). One brush shared by all 7 TabToggleWidgets in
       TAOMFaceGen.xml's ribbon - the widget itself carries no sprite/background, just this text child, and
       relies on UpdateChildrenStates="true" (set on each TabToggleWidget) to propagate its own Selected/Hovered
       interaction state down to this brush, the same mechanism CC.BtnText already relies on for Back/Next. -->
  <Brush Name="CC.TabText" Font="FS_CinzelWide" FontSize="16" TextHorizontalAlignment="Center" TextVerticalAlignment="Center">
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default" FontColor="#8F8670FF" TextGlowColor="#000000B0" TextGlowRadius="0.15" TextBlur="0.1" />
      <Style Name="Hovered" FontColor="#D9CBA0FF" TextGlowColor="#000000B0" TextGlowRadius="0.15" TextBlur="0.1" />
      <Style Name="Pressed" FontColor="#F6E7B4FF" TextGlowColor="#000000C0" TextGlowRadius="0.2" TextBlur="0.1" />
      <Style Name="Selected" FontColor="#F6E7B4FF" TextGlowColor="#000000C0" TextGlowRadius="0.2" TextBlur="0.1" />
    </Styles>
  </Brush>

  <!-- small diamond marker under the active ribbon tab (2026-09-23, Phase 3 polish). TabToggleWidget has no
       bindable @IsSelected of its own to drive an IsVisible - it only propagates Default/Hovered/Pressed/
       Selected STYLE STATE to children via UpdateChildrenStates="true" (same mechanism CC.TabText already
       relies on), so this is a brush (alpha-only per state) on a small child ImageWidget, not a data binding. -->
  <Brush Name="CC.TabAccent">
    <Layers><BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="fs_bullet" /></Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.35" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Selected"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" /></Style>
    </Styles>
  </Brush>

  <!-- Back/Next pill buttons (2026-09-23 redesign, replaces CC.BtnBack/CC.BtnNext below - those are kept,
       unused, in case of a revert). Copied from FactionSelect.xml's Preview.Confirm/Preview.ConfirmText
       verbatim - same fs_confirm sprite, already deployed, no new art. -->
  <Brush Name="CC.Confirm">
    <Layers><BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="fs_confirm" /></Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" ColorFactor="1.2" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" ColorFactor="0.85" /></Style>
      <!-- Added 2026-09-25 for the Review Stage's Next button, whose @CanAdvance can genuinely be false in a
           way the user needs to notice (empty/invalid name field) - every earlier screen using this brush
           always had CanAdvance effectively true-looking with no visible feedback either way, so this gap
           existed but was never actually exercised until now. -->
      <Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.4" /></Style>
    </Styles>
  </Brush>
  <Brush Name="CC.ConfirmText" Font="FS_CinzelWide" FontSize="22" TextHorizontalAlignment="Center" TextVerticalAlignment="Center">
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default" FontColor="#DEC98FFF" TextGlowColor="#000000A0" TextGlowRadius="0.1" TextBlur="0.05" />
      <Style Name="Hovered" FontColor="#F2E2B0FF" TextGlowColor="#000000A0" TextGlowRadius="0.1" TextBlur="0.05" />
      <Style Name="Pressed" FontColor="#C9AB69FF" TextGlowColor="#000000A0" TextGlowRadius="0.1" TextBlur="0.05" />
      <Style Name="Disabled" FontColor="#DEC98FFF" TextAlphaFactor="0.4" />
    </Styles>
  </Brush>

  <!-- Same colours/glow as CC.ConfirmText, smaller FontSize - TAOMNarrativeStage.xml's Back/Next/Random
       buttons are shrunk from FaceGen's own Confirm-button size to fit three across the gap between its two
       side panels (2026-09-26, user: "make the text a little bit smaller so that they fit better inside the
       buttons"), so they need their own smaller text scale. A dedicated brush rather than editing
       CC.ConfirmText directly, since that brush is shared with FaceGen's own full-size Confirm buttons, which
       fit fine as-is and weren't asked to change. -->
  <Brush Name="CC.ConfirmTextSmall" Font="FS_CinzelWide" FontSize="15" TextHorizontalAlignment="Center" TextVerticalAlignment="Center">
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default" FontColor="#DEC98FFF" TextGlowColor="#000000A0" TextGlowRadius="0.1" TextBlur="0.05" />
      <Style Name="Hovered" FontColor="#F2E2B0FF" TextGlowColor="#000000A0" TextGlowRadius="0.1" TextBlur="0.05" />
      <Style Name="Pressed" FontColor="#C9AB69FF" TextGlowColor="#000000A0" TextGlowRadius="0.1" TextBlur="0.05" />
      <Style Name="Disabled" FontColor="#DEC98FFF" TextAlphaFactor="0.4" />
    </Styles>
  </Brush>

  <!-- Translucent variant of CC.Confirm for TAOMNarrativeStage.xml's Back/Next only (2026-09-26, user: "still
       has no opacity on the background of those buttons" - CC.Confirm itself is Default AlphaFactor=1, fully
       opaque, and is shared with FaceGen's/Review Stage's own Confirm buttons which weren't asked to change,
       hence a dedicated brush rather than editing CC.Confirm directly). Same fs_confirm sprite/ColorFactor
       hover-brighten behaviour, just lower alpha at rest so it reads consistent with the option rows' own
       translucent look (CC.NarrativeOptionTextFrame) that the user just confirmed looks good. -->
  <Brush Name="CC.NarrativeConfirm">
    <Layers><BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="fs_confirm" /></Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.55" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.85" ColorFactor="1.2" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" ColorFactor="0.85" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.35" /></Style>
    </Styles>
  </Brush>

  <!-- Random button background (2026-09-30, user: "the button doesnt look like its in the same style as the
       rest" - TAOMNarrativeStage.xml's Random button, sitting between Back/Next). It couldn't just reuse
       CC.NarrativeConfirm/fs_confirm like Back/Next do: fs_confirm is a wide decorative banner with thin
       tapering line flourishes baked into its art at a fixed ~7.27:1 aspect ratio, and the gap between Back's
       right edge and Next's left edge (~248px) is narrower than fs_confirm would need at a legible height
       (~291px at 40px tall) - stretching it to fit would visibly warp those flourishes. It had instead been
       using CC.NarrativeOptionTextFrame, a flat single-color BlankWhiteSquare_9 wash with square corners and
       no real border art (itself a leftover brush, marked unused elsewhere in this file since round 13) - a
       plain rectangle next to two ornate pill banners, which is what read as "different style". cc_section_9
       is a NATIVE Bannerlord sprite (no custom art needed - already used by this project's own CC.DropList for
       FaceGen's dropdown panels), a proper nine-sliced bordered box that can resize to any aspect ratio without
       distorting, so it actually looks like real game UI here instead of a flat color swatch. -->
  <!-- #704 port: cc_section_9 ships nowhere (not in Kysaro's package, the game GUI or any module), so this and CC.DropList use his cc_card_9, the nine-sliced card CC.DropItem already uses. Ask Kysaro for cc_section.png to restore the original look. -->
  <Brush Name="CC.NarrativeRandomBox">
    <Layers><BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="cc_card_9" /></Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.7" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" ColorFactor="1.2" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" ColorFactor="0.85" /></Style>
    </Styles>
  </Brush>

  <!-- selection cards (gender, hair and beard grids) -->
  <Brush Name="CC.Card">
    <Layers>
      <BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="cc_card_9" />
      <BrushLayer Name="Selected" Sprite="cc_card_sel_9" />
    </Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="1" /><BrushLayer Name="Selected" IsHidden="true" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="1.5" /><BrushLayer Name="Selected" IsHidden="true" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="0.8" /><BrushLayer Name="Selected" IsHidden="true" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Selected"><BrushLayer Name="Default" IsHidden="true" /><BrushLayer Name="Selected" ColorFactor="1" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.5" /><BrushLayer Name="Selected" IsHidden="true" /></Style>
    </Styles>
    <SoundProperties><EventSounds><EventSound EventName="Click" Audio="checkbox" /></EventSounds></SoundProperties>
  </Brush>

  <Brush Name="CC.GenderM">
    <Layers><BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="cc_g_male" /></Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.7" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.8" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Selected"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" ColorFactor="1.2" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.4" /></Style>
    </Styles>
  </Brush>
  <Brush Name="CC.GenderF">
    <Layers><BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="cc_g_female" /></Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.7" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.8" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Selected"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" ColorFactor="1.2" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.4" /></Style>
    </Styles>
  </Brush>

  <!-- Gender button ring (2026-09-26, exact-match reference request: circular gender buttons instead of the
       square CC.Card frame). cc_gender_ring/_sel are procedurally-drawn thin gold rings (System.Drawing, not
       AI-generated - simple geometric shapes don't need it), mirroring CC.Card's exact Default/Selected/Hovered/
       Pressed/Disabled layer-swap pattern so the button still gets a real Selected-state visual. -->
  <Brush Name="CC.GenderRing">
    <Layers>
      <BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="cc_gender_ring" />
      <BrushLayer Name="Selected" Sprite="cc_gender_ring_sel" />
    </Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="1" /><BrushLayer Name="Selected" IsHidden="true" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="1.5" /><BrushLayer Name="Selected" IsHidden="true" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" ColorFactor="0.8" /><BrushLayer Name="Selected" IsHidden="true" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Selected"><BrushLayer Name="Default" IsHidden="true" /><BrushLayer Name="Selected" ColorFactor="1" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.5" /><BrushLayer Name="Selected" IsHidden="true" /></Style>
    </Styles>
    <SoundProperties><EventSounds><EventSound EventName="Click" Audio="checkbox" /></EventSounds></SoundProperties>
  </Brush>
  <!-- centered small-caps label under a gender ring/tool icon - CC.SecTitle is Left-aligned (built for
       full-width section headers), so this is a separate Center-aligned brush rather than reusing it. -->
  <Brush Name="CC.IconLabel" Font="FS_CinzelWide" FontSize="13" TextHorizontalAlignment="Center" TextVerticalAlignment="Center">
    <Styles><Style Name="Default" FontColor="#D9BC78FF" TextGlowColor="#000000B0" TextGlowRadius="0.15" TextBlur="0.1" /></Styles>
  </Brush>
  <!-- smaller variant for the tools row, where 7 icons (vs the gender row's 2) leave much tighter horizontal
       room per label. -->
  <Brush Name="CC.ToolLabel" Font="FS_CinzelWide" FontSize="10" TextHorizontalAlignment="Center" TextVerticalAlignment="Center">
    <Styles><Style Name="Default" FontColor="#B8A876FF" TextGlowColor="#000000B0" TextGlowRadius="0.15" TextBlur="0.1" /></Styles>
  </Brush>

  <!-- tool strip buttons (one brush per glyph) -->
  <Brush Name="CC.Tool.Random"><Layers><BrushLayer Name="Glyph" Sprite="cc_g_random" /></Layers>
    <Styles><Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Glyph" AlphaFactor="0.8" /></Style><Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Glyph" AlphaFactor="1" ColorFactor="1.3" /></Style><Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Glyph" AlphaFactor="0.7" /></Style><Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Glyph" AlphaFactor="0.3" /></Style></Styles>
    <SoundProperties><EventSounds><EventSound EventName="Click" Audio="transfer" /></EventSounds></SoundProperties></Brush>
  <Brush Name="CC.Tool.RandomAll"><Layers><BrushLayer Name="Glyph" Sprite="cc_g_random_all" /></Layers>
    <Styles><Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Glyph" AlphaFactor="0.8" /></Style><Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Glyph" AlphaFactor="1" ColorFactor="1.3" /></Style><Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Glyph" AlphaFactor="0.7" /></Style><Style Name="Disabled"><BrushLayer Name="Glyph" AlphaFactor="0.3" /></Style></Styles>
