       rectangular shape also, i gues we can get rid of that?"): the row's own background wash (this brush,
       covering the whole row) was still showing faintly at rest behind the new text box, reading as a stray
       leftover rectangle now that framing is handled explicitly by the text box itself. Default alpha dropped
       to 0 (fully invisible at rest). FIX round 4 (user: "when hovering over them i can still see the ugly
       brownish rectangular shape from before... nice they have a little effect when hovering but not that
       one"): Hovered/Pressed/Selected were still using their old alpha values, so the exact wash just asked to
       be removed was still appearing on hover/selection. Dropped ALL states to 0 - this brush no longer draws
       anything at all. Hover/selection feedback now comes entirely from CC.NarrativeOptionTextFrame below
       (the text box's own border brightening) plus the pre-existing accent bar and text-color change, not from
       a whole-row wash. -->
  <!-- Option row text-box fill (round 13 replacement for the separate CC.NarrativeOptionTextFrame border,
       see that brush's own note): the state-driven hover/selected brighten now lives directly on the
       fs_tile_stone_9 texture itself via AlphaFactor/ColorFactor, so there's only ever ONE border - the
       texture's own baked-in gold edge - not two overlapping ones. -->
  <Brush Name="CC.NarrativeOptionFill">
    <!-- FIX round 16 (user, marked up screenshot: still a visible thick double border - fs_tile_stone_9's own
         baked-in gold edge was STILL bleeding through even at a 14px inset; round 15's fix only added a second,
         correctly-thin border alongside it, it didn't remove the first one). Swapped to ld_bar_stone - same
         dark stone material/look, used elsewhere in this project as a loading-bar fill, but with NO gold edge
         baked in and no .nine sidecar at all (plain stretch, zero 9-slice scaling ambiguity to fight this
         time). The hand-built 2px bars from round 15 are now the ONLY border. -->
    <Layers><BrushLayer Name="Default" Sprite="ld_bar_stone" /></Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="0.85" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Hovered"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" ColorFactor="1.15" /></Style>
      <Style Name="Pressed"><BrushLayer Name="Default" AlphaFactor="1" ColorFactor="0.9" /></Style>
